  "id": "COMPOUND:19392 - PROTEIN:5790",
  "verbalization": "Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether is implicated in the interaction with HPAC through multiple pathways, with the primary mechanism involving the MIP (macrophage inflammatory protein) as a common intermediate. The drug targets MIP, which in turn is targeted by various compounds, including 7-hydroxy-6-(2-(R)-hydroxy-3-methylbut-3-enyl)coumarin and 5-hydroxy-6,8-dimethoxy-2,3-dimethylbenzo[G]chromen-4-one. These compounds, in turn, have HPAC as their target, suggesting a hierarchical pathway where Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether may influence HPAC through the MIP pathway. The evidence supports a potential role for Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether in modulating HPAC activity via the MIP system, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the drug-target relationship, emphasizing the importance of further investigation into the molecular mechanisms underlying this interaction.",
